# The production Caddyfile (spec §19.1; plan M5 Task 21, Deviation 34), mounted read-only with caddy/site.caddy
# beside it. The domain and the ACME contact come from the caddy service's environment (§19.2).
#
# - HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 only: port 443 is published over TCP alone, so HTTP/3 is never advertised (no Alt-Svc).
# - Caddy has no access log (caddy/site.caddy). The lines it still writes, its errors among them (a 502 while
#   the api restarts names the request), go through a filter that deletes the client's address, port and
#   request headers: client addresses are personal data.
{
	email {$JOBHUNTER_ACME_EMAIL}
	servers {
		protocols h1 h2
	}
	log default {
		format filter {
			wrap json
			request>remote_ip delete
			request>remote_port delete
			request>client_ip delete
			request>headers delete
		}
	}
}

{$JOBHUNTER_DOMAIN} {
	import site.caddy
}
